{
  "notes": "Electro-funk, E dorian, 108 BPM, nearly straight sixteenths. Casio-style synth brass (CZ BRASS) stabbing two-note shells (3rd and 7th) around the kick, a square-wave funk bass that lands on the one with fifths, sevenths and slides, the player's talkbox on the Smart Keys (glide, the vowel moving with MOTION), and the ELECTRO kit: syncopated 808 kick, snare and clap on 2 and 4, accented sixteenth hats, a cowbell, FM toms in the fills, the parts ducking under the kick. The bass sits on E2 so the roots stay in range; the progressions use only i, ii, III and IV. Scenes: A BOOT UP holds Em7 with long brass chords; B GROOVE vamps i7 IV7 (Em7 A7); C OVERDRIVE walks down IV7 III ii7 i7 in half bars with open hats; D COOL DOWN rests on ii7 IV7. ENERGY: brass alone, then kick and bass, then the full electro kit in eighths, then sixteenths, fills and ratchets. All material is original.",
